## What to check

Pick the 3-7 most consequential claims in the report and, for each, verify:
- The reference URL is reachable and returns readable content.
- The cited content actually supports the claim made in the report.

## Budget and termination — IMPORTANT

- Use AT MOST 10 `read_url` calls total, even if the report cites more sources.  Skim — don't read every source exhaustively.
{% if terminal_fact_check | default(false) %}
- Call `read_url` AT MOST ONCE per URL that was actually fetched. Do not re-fetch a URL you have already read.
- After your checks, your **final response must be a brief summary** with no further tool calls. Note unsupported claims, mismatches, or links that an actual fetch showed unavailable. A link not found through independent search or denied before fetch is unverified, not proven dead. Otherwise note "all checked references support their claims." This summary is what your caller will see — make sure it is informative and self-contained.
{% else %}
